# INVWINCA.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: Export CSV at
# level 3.  The file name dialog lists C:\RUN's files *.CSV; a name
# typed goes into the form as a path, where LOCS is chosen, and the
# export's message box says how many records it wrote.  The same file,
# chosen in the list, again with the field names: the question whether
# to replace it, No going back to the form, then Yes.  A name the server
# refuses (a .DBF) on the form's message line, mended in the form to a
# name without a directory, which the engine takes from the current
# directory, given back by the dialog; Cancel in the file name dialog
# and in the form, each sending nothing; after the dialog listed DATA
# and was cancelled, CATS exported to a name without a directory, which
# the engine writes into C:\RUN only when the dialog gave the program's
# directory back; LTYPES, the location types, exported with the
# dialog's name; the end by Exit.  The run must leave CALOCS.CSV,
# CAITEMS.CSV, CABARE.CSV and CALTYPES.CSV equal to their goldens in
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINCA.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER ALT-A E
S NAME
T calocs.csv
K ENTER
S FORM
K DOWN ENTER
S WRITTEN
K ENTER ALT-A E TAB HOME
S CHOSEN
K ENTER DOWN TAB TAB SPACE
S HEADER
K ENTER
S REPLACEQ
K N
S KEPT
K ENTER
S AGAIN
K Y
S REPLACED
K ENTER ALT-A E
T ITEMS.DBF
K ENTER ENTER
S REFUSED
T CAITEMS.CSV
K ENTER
S ITEMS
K ENTER ALT-A E ESC
S NOFILE
K ALT-A E ENTER
S PATTERN
T X.CSV
K ENTER ESC
S NOFORM
K ALT-A E
T DATA
K ENTER ESC ALT-A E
T X.CSV
K ENTER DOWN DOWN TAB
T CABARE.CSV
S BAREFORM
K ENTER
S BARE
K ENTER ALT-A E
T CALTYPES.CSV
K ENTER DOWN DOWN DOWN
S LTFORM
K ENTER
S LTYPES
K ENTER ALT-F X
